is: Confirmed on each page: PEP 744 "about as fast as the existing specializing interpreter on most platforms" and "about 10-20% more memory"; the 3.15 page (section past character 100,000, headed "Upgraded experimental JIT compiler") gives 7-8% on x86-64 Linux and 11-12% on AArch64 macOS and "Python 3.15 was released on 9 October 2026"; LWN 2026-09-01 reports the June pause of new JIT development on main with a six-month window; PEP 836 header reads Withdrawn, resolution 19-Oct-2026. Of the thread this review reached only the first page and post 75 (2026-10-29).
by: r3/review-self-compiling-systems
at: 2026-11-24

